1.   CANADIAN EMBASSY HAS PROVIDED FOLLOWING LIST OF THOSE
ACCOMPANYING PRIMIN HOVEYDA TO CANADA DEC. 9-14:
JAFAR NADIM, MFA, UNDERSEC. FOR INTERNATIONAL AND
ECON. AFFAIRS;
AKBAR ETEMAD (NOT MANOUCHEHR EGHBAL AS REPORTED
EARLIER), PRESIDENT, IRANIAN ATOMIC ENERGY ORG.
AND ASSISTANT TO PRIMIN;
PARVIZ RADJI, SPECIAL ADVISOR TO PRIMIN;
HASSANALI MEHRAN, DEPUTY MIN. ECON. AND FINANCE;
MISS AFSANEH M JAHANBANI, PRIMIN'S PRIVATE SECRETARY;
MRS. FERESHTEH ENSHA, PERSONAL PHYSICAN;
CAPT. GHASSEM NILI, CHIEF SECURITY OFFICER;
CAPT. SEIFOLLAH TAHERI, SECURITY OFFICER;
MOHAMMAD SIAMAKI, PERSONAL VALET;
IRAJ GORGIN, NATIONAL IRANIAN RADIO AND TELEVISION ORG.;
AMIR TAHERI, EDITOR, KAYHAN NEWSPAPER;
MOHAMMAD POURDAD, TEHRAN JOURNAL.
2. MOST OF PARTY WILL FLY DIRECTLY TO CANADA. WE WILL PROVIDE
HOVEYDA'S ARRIVAL TIME IN NEW YORK DEC. 7 AS SOON
AS AVAILABLE SO APPROPRIATE COURTESIES CAN BE EXTENDED.
MIKLOS

B) MEXICO 10695
1.  MEXICO CITY PRESS REPORTS THAT MRS. MARIA ESTER ZUNO DE
ECHEVERRIA, THE PRESIDENT OF MEXICO'S WIFE, WILL DEPART VERACRUZ
JANUARY 2 AS THE HEAD OF A LARGE CULTURAL AND ECONOMIC MISSION
WHICH WILL INCLUDE ALMOST 400 MEXICAN MUSICIANS, ARTISTS, AND
DANCERS AS WELL AS A COLLECTION OF 105 PAINTINGS BY 50 OF MEXICO'S
MOST FAMOUS ARTISTS. THE MISSION WHICH WILL TRAVEL ON TWO
FERRY BOATS, HAS THE FOLLOWING ITINERARY:
HAVANA, CUBA, JANUARY 4-10;
KINGSTON, JAMAICA, JANUARY 21-15;
LA GUAIRA, VENEZUELA, JANUARY 17-23;
CROSS PANAMA CANAL, JANUARY 25;
PUNTA ARENAS, COSTA RICA, JANUARY 27;
SAN JOSE, COSTA RICA, JANUARY 28-30;
PUNTA ARENAS, COSTA RICA, JANUARY 31;
ACAPULCO, MEXICO, FEBRUARY 2.
JOVA

RESERVATIONS MADE HOTEL RITZ.  SINGLE DOLLARS 21;
DOUBLE DOLLARS 27.
BLOOMFIELD

